From: JingMatrix <jingmatrix@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 22:51:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 24/47] Harvest device identifiers and the module hash

The identifiers a real attestation carries, which the device-properties path
omits, are read straight from the platform: IMEI and MEID from the IPhoneSubInfo
binder's legacy getDeviceIdForPhone/getMeidForSubscriber calls, and the serial
from the ro.serialno property. The public TelephonyManager.getImei and
Build.getSerial paths are deliberately avoided - they enforce a "calling package
belongs to the caller uid" check the root daemon (uid 0, no package) can never
satisfy, while the legacy binder calls return the real values regardless.

Also derive the module hash the way the main branch does, and mark IMEI, serial
and the module hash as fabricated when they are not actually attested, so the
harvest panel can show which values are real captures and which are stand-ins.
Each parsed field is logged.
